nftables: the xtables MARK target and mark and multiport matches

What: rules that iptables-nft writes through nft_compat with the MARK target
(revision 2, xt_mark_tginfo2: mark = (mark & ~mask) ^ value) and the mark
(revision 1, xt_mark_mtinfo1: (mark & mask) == value, possibly inverted) and
multiport (revision 1, xt_multiport_v1: up to 15 source, destination or either
ports and ranges, possibly inverted) matches are taken and evaluated as
net/netfilter/xt_mark.c and net/netfilter/xt_multiport.c do, instead of
failing. Like Linux, MARK and mark take any family and table, multiport IPv4
and IPv6; their info is taken when it is at least the struct's size and the
same once aligned (XT_ALIGN), multiport's flags and count are checked as in
multiport_mt_check(), an unknown revision is EPROTONOSUPPORT as in
xt_find_revision(), ranges are checked as in multiport_valid_ranges() (a port
flagged as a range's start must be followed by its end, not flagged and not
below it; else EINVAL), and a multiport match never takes a packet that is not
TCP or UDP or a fragment other than the first, reads the ports of an IPv4
datagram's first fragment where its transport header begins, as
skb_header_pointer() does, and drops a packet too short to hold its ports
(hotdrop).

Why: the CNI portmap plugin publishes a port with "-m multiport -p tcp
--destination-ports <port>" and marks connections from the host for
masquerading with "-j MARK --set-xmark 0x2000/0x2000" and "-m mark --mark
0x2000/0x2000"; netavark's iptables driver uses the same marks. Every port
Podman's CNI backend published failed: "Warning: Extension MARK revision 0
not supported, missing kernel module?", then "Extension multiport revision 0
not supported".

Not done: Linux's multiport_mt_check() also refuses a rule that does not
match one of these protocols first; gVisor's nft_compat does not know a
rule's protocol, so the check is at the packet.

Upstream: none found; drop this patch when upstream has these extensions.

Verified:
- The new unit tests TestCompatMarkTargetEvaluation (--set-xmark,
  --set-mark, --or-mark, --and-mark, --xor-mark), TestCompatMarkParse,
  TestCompatMarkMatchEvaluation and TestCompatMultiportMatch (ports, ranges,
  source, destination, either, inversion, another protocol, the first and a
  later fragment of a datagram, malformed info, an unterminated, a reversed
  and a doubly flagged range)
  pass with the rest of //pkg/tcpip/nftables:nftables_test in gVisor's builder
  container. socket_netlink_netfilter_test passes on runsc with
  --TESTONLY-nftables --net-raw (268 tests).
- Podman 4.9.3's CNI backend in an Ubuntu 24.04 sandbox under runsc-nested
  published a port that answered on the sandbox's loopback and its own
  address.

